# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs. Without this, `docker
# build .` ships the whole working tree - including `.venv/` and `.git/` - to the
# daemon before the first layer runs, which on a synced-folder checkout dominates the
# build time. Cloud Build's `--source .` upload falls back to `.gitignore` semantics
# and so already skipped `.venv/`, but a local `docker build` had no such fallback.
#
# Every path COPYd by the Dockerfile must stay OUT of this file: pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, README.md, src/, ground_rules/, tests/golden/, desk/data/, memos/.

.venv/
.git/
.github/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Working and output trees the image never reads. `desk/data/` is the snapshot the desk
# serves and is deliberately not listed here; `data/` and `artefacts/` are the index
# builder's local inputs and outputs, which the container regenerates or does without.
data/
artefacts/
notebooks/
docs/
communications/
.superpowers/
